### Generative / set-level matching
- K026: SET-LEVEL DISTRIBUTION MATCHING NEEDS SAME-CELL SETS OR VARYING COMPOSITION (N034-B v2): linear readout on frozen SSL LF features (n007, transductive unlabelled pretraining) learnt only from set-level information (bag-mean ridge / 1-D OT), clean v5c labels, new-draw split 2, mean r over 7 targets: paired .561; SAME cells with pairing hidden, random sets of 4/16/64/256/2048: .548/.503/.451/.309/.104 (lineage markers ~97 % at 16, autofl/CD19 50-60 %); DIFFERENT cells of the same slide, random or same-FOV groups: no positive recovery with any learner/size (mean |r| .05-.15 of both signs = FOV-level components, max .48; no permutation null). The first (OT-only) bench understated large same-cell sets (learner failure, red-team N4 reproduced: synthetic OT .03 vs bag-mean .99). Scope: these learners/designs, 1 run, large-n decline partly few-bag regression [partial] (N034; .agent-research/results/N034-lf-fluorescence-marker-images-by-conditi/setmatch/setmatch_sim_v2.csv) {cites:0}
- K027: LF -> FLUORESCENCE IMAGES BY CONDITIONAL FLOW MATCHING (N034-A, 28 M UNet, patch-2, b1->b0, 1 seed): per-cell r needs >= 48 Heun steps + CFG 2-3 (16 steps under-disperse); distribution scores already beat regression at s16 g2 or s48 g1 (s16 g1 wins CRPS only). At s48 g2-3: distributionally better than the same net as regression (DEVELOPMENT numbers, sampler chosen on them; new draw CRPS .57 vs .78, conditional W1 .55 vs .74; rank calibration still fails, outside-fraction .77 vs .40; marginal W1 is passed by an LF-shuffled control, so only conditional scores count), equal per cell on lineage markers (CD16 .86, CD14 .86, CD45 .76) but worse on subtle ones (CD3 .25 vs .55, HLA-DR .36 vs .50; mean .55 vs .61). Image targets: border-median bg, smooth position gain kept only if it generalises to held-out FOVs (72/132; the HGB gain fitted FOV-composition noise) CONFIRMED by the frozen pre-registered reverse-direction test N035 (train draw 0, untouched draw-1 split 1, sampler frozen at s48 g2): CRPS .674 vs .815, condW1 .692 vs .727 (7/12 labels), r .476 vs .576 (worse on all 12), outside .53 vs ideal .22; on a new draw CFG 2 over-disperses (sd ratio 1.25). HLA-DR's real-image readout does not transfer between draws (r -.11) [1 seed per direction, readout yardstick] (N034; .agent-research/results/N034-lf-fluorescence-marker-images-by-conditi/n034_sampler_sweep.csv; N035; .agent-research/results/N035-frozen-confirmation-of-n034-a-in-the-unt/n035_means.csv) {cites:0}

